# Phase 4: Billing Views & Reporting

## Goal
Build all billing views that Joyce uses daily: payment lists, monthly summaries, cash flow reports, invoices, statements, and PDF exports.

## Build Order

### 1. All Payments View (`/admin/billing/payments`)
- TanStack Table with columns: date, contact (company), amount, method, check #, purchase (invoice #)
- Filters: year (select), search (contact name/company)
- Sorting: date (default desc), amount, contact
- Pagination: 25 per page
- Query: join payments → purchases → contacts to display contact info

### 2. This Month View (`/admin/billing/this-month`)
- Table of scheduled payments due this month (or overdue from past months)
- Columns: contact, invoice #, due date, amount due, amount paid (computed), status (paid/partial/overdue/upcoming)
- Late indicator: red badge if `isScheduledPaymentLate()` returns true
- Year filter dropdown
- Quick action: record payment directly from this view
- Query uses the billing helpers from Phase 3 — never stores status

### 3. Cash Flow Report (`/admin/billing/cash-flow`)
- Grid layout: rows = contacts, columns = months (Jan-Dec) + Year Total
- Each cell shows: projected (scheduled payment amount) vs actual (sum of allocations for that month)
- Color coding: green (paid in full), yellow (partial), red (unpaid/overdue), gray (no payment due)
- Scoped by calendar edition year (dropdown filter) — this fixes the v1 bug where it mixed years
- Summary row at bottom: totals per month
- PDF export button

### 4. Invoice View (`/admin/purchases/[id]/invoice`)
- Printable layout (full page, clean formatting)
- Header: operator business info, logo
- Bill To: contact info (company, name, address)
- Invoice #: from purchase
- Line items: each ad purchase with calendar, ad type, quantity, unit price, total
- Subtotals: total sale, discounts, additional sales, trade
- Net amount
- Payment terms: due day, early discount info, late fee info
- Custom messages: invoice message from payment terms
- Print button + Download PDF button

### 5. Statement View (`/admin/contacts/[id]/statement`)
- Contact info header
- Table of all purchases across editions with:
  - Invoice #, edition, year, net amount, amount paid (computed), balance (computed)
- Payment history table: all payments with date, amount, method, which purchase
- Overall balance: sum of all unpaid amounts
- Custom statement message from payment terms
- Print + PDF download

### 6. PDF Generation (`src/lib/pdf/`)
Create reusable PDF generator using pdf-lib:
- `generateInvoicePdf(purchase, contact, paymentTerms, adPurchases)` → Uint8Array
- `generateCashFlowPdf(report, edition, year)` → Uint8Array
- `generateStatementPdf(contact, purchases, payments)` → Uint8Array
- Serve via Next.js API route that returns PDF as download

### 7. Email Integration (Resend)
- `src/lib/email/send-invoice.ts` — send invoice email with PDF attachment
- `src/lib/email/send-statement.ts` — send statement email
- React Email templates in `src/emails/`:
  - `invoice-email.tsx` — clean invoice email template
  - `statement-email.tsx` — statement email template
- Trigger from UI: "Email Invoice" button on purchase detail, "Email Statement" on contact detail

## Important Rules
- ALL financial figures come from the Phase 3 computed helpers — never raw database fields
- Cash flow report must be scoped by edition year — this was a critical v1 bug
- PDF generation happens server-side (API route or Convex action)
- Currency formatting: use consistent `formatCurrency()` utility from `src/lib/utils.ts`
- Date formatting: use consistent `formatDate()` utility
